# syscall_aarch64_linux.cyr — aarch64 wrapper backfill for stdlib gaps
#
# Self-gated with `#ifdef CYRIUS_ARCH_AARCH64` so this file ships in
# the bundled `dist/phylax.cyr` alongside the x86_64 peer; only the
# matching arch's block compiles in any given consumer build.
#
# ⚠ CURRENTLY EMPTY BY DESIGN — do not delete the file.
#
# Until 1.3.0 this held `var SYS_RENAMEAT = 38;` and a `sys_rename` composed
# through renameat(AT_FDCWD, old, AT_FDCWD, new), written when cyrius 5.10.x's
# aarch64 peer had no rename at all. The stdlib now ships that exact wrapper
# (`lib/syscalls_aarch64_linux.cyr`, `sys_rename` → `sys_renameat`), so the
# local copy only produced a `duplicate fn 'sys_rename'` warning on every
# aarch64 build. Removed. Keep any future gap here as an arch-gated function,
# never as a `var SYS_* = <number>` (see src/syscall_x86_64_linux.cyr).

#ifdef CYRIUS_ARCH_AARCH64

#endif
